3. Playwright configuration
File: playwright.config.js

Humne configuration mein ye features set kiye:
- Test directory: ./tests
- Fully parallel execution
- CI ke liye retries
- HTML reporter
- Trace on first retry
- Three browser projects

import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';
import { envConfig } from './config/envConfig.js';

export default defineConfig({
  testDir: './tests',
  fullyParallel: true,
  forbidOnly: !!process.env.CI,
  retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
  workers: process.env.CI ? 1 : undefined,
  reporter: 'html',

  use: {
    baseURL: envConfig.baseURL,
    trace: 'on-first-retry',
  },

  projects: [
    {
      name: 'chromium',
      use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] },
    },
    {
      name: 'firefox',
      use: { ...devices['Desktop Firefox'] },
    },
    {
      name: 'webkit',
      use: { ...devices['Desktop Safari'] },
    },
  ],
});



Important concepts:
- baseURL – application ka base URL.
- fullyParallel – tests parallel execute kar sakta hai.
- retries – failed tests ko dobara run karta hai.
- reporter – test results ka report generate karta hai.
- projects – multiple browsers configure karta hai.
4. Page Object Model (POM)
Humne SauceDemo login page ke liye LoginPage.js banayi.

File: pages/LoginPage.js

export class LoginPage {
  constructor(page) {
    this.page = page;

    this.usernameInput = page.locator('[data-test="username"]');
    this.passwordInput = page.locator('[data-test="password"]');
    this.loginButton = page.locator('[data-test="login-button"]');
    this.errorMessage = page.locator('[data-test="error"]');
  }

  async open() {
    await this.page.goto('/');
  }

  async login(username, password) {
    await this.usernameInput.fill(username);
    await this.passwordInput.fill(password);
    await this.loginButton.click();
  }
}



POM kya hai?

Page Object Model ek design pattern hai jisme page ke locators aur actions ko alag class mein rakhte hain.

Benefits:
- Code reusability
- Easy maintenance
- Less duplication
- Clean test files
5. Test Data Management
File: test-data/loginData.js
export const loginData = {
  validUser: {
    username: 'standard_user',
    password: 'secret_sauce',
  },
};


Iska purpose test data ko test cases se alag rakhna hai.

Agar username ya password change karna ho toh test file edit karne ki zaroorat nahi.
6. Custom Fixtures
File: fixtures/testFixtures.js
import { test as base } from '@playwright/test';
import { LoginPage } from '../pages/LoginPage.js';

export const test = base.extend({
  loginPage: async ({ page }, use) => {
    const loginPage = new LoginPage(page);

    await loginPage.open();

    await use(loginPage);
  },
});

export { expect } from '@playwright/test';


Fixture kya hota hai?

Fixture reusable setup provide karta hai.

Hamare case mein:
1. Browser page milta hai.
2. LoginPage object create hota hai.
3. Login page automatically open hota hai.
4. Test ko loginPage fixture milta hai.
Isse har test mein baar-baar login page open karne ka code nahi likhna padta.
7. UI Automation Testing
File: tests/ui/login.spec.js

Humne 3 test cases create kiye:
Test case	Expected result
Login page open	Username, password aur login button visible
Valid login	Inventory page open
Invalid password	Error message visible

Important Playwright assertions:
await expect(locator).toBeVisible();

await expect(page).toHaveURL(/inventory.html/);

await expect(locator).toContainText('Username and password do not match');


UI test command:
npx playwright test tests/ui/login.spec.js --project=chromium


3 UI tests passed
8. API Automation Framework
Humne API testing ke liye JSONPlaceholder demo API use ki.

Base URL:
https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com


ApiClient.js
File: api/ApiClient.js

Is class mein reusable HTTP methods banaye:
Method	Purpose
get()	Data retrieve
post()	New data create
put()	Existing data update
delete()	Data delete

Code:

export class ApiClient {
  constructor(request, baseURL) {
    this.request = request;
    this.baseURL = baseURL;
  }

  async get(endpoint) {
    return await this.request.get(
      `${this.baseURL}${endpoint}`
    );
  }

  async post(endpoint, data) {
    return await this.request.post(
      `${this.baseURL}${endpoint}`,
      { data }
    );
  }

  async put(endpoint, data) {
    return await this.request.put(
      `${this.baseURL}${endpoint}`,
      { data }
    );
  }

  async delete(endpoint) {
    return await this.request.delete(
      `${this.baseURL}${endpoint}`
    );
  }
}



Important: ApiClient ko api/ folder mein rakha hai, utils/ mein nahi, kyunki ye specifically API operations handle karta hai.
9. API Configuration
